$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure G. Reaction of amine
compounds with acylating agents. Amine (1 equiv.) was purged with argon,
dissolved in pyridine (0.2 M), and cooled to 0 °C. Acylating agent (1
equiv.) was added, and the reaction mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 3 h.
Saturated NaHCO3 was added, and the reaction mixture was extracted with 4
x 5 mL of DCM. The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. Compounds were purified using basic or acidic
conditions via preparative chromatography. Cmpd # 46b{2}, yield 83%.
Formula:C24H25F3N3O3, M +:H, calcd mass: 460.1843, found mass: 460.1841,
purity: 96.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of a γ-Lactam Library via Formal Cycloaddition of Imines and
