$DATUM 1,22,25-Triacetyl-1,22,25-triaza-3,6:17,20-dibenzo-7,10,13,16-tetraoxoheteroeycleheptaeosane
(1a) Compound 1 (1.28 g, 3 mol) was dissolved in CHCl3 (5 mL), and then
absolute pyridine (2mL) was added. The mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 5 min. (CH3CO)2O (2mL) was added to the pale yellow
solution, and it was stirred at room temperature for 6 h. After the
reaction was complete, the solution was poured into 50 mL of light
petroleum (60-90°C): a white precipitate was formed and collected by
filtration. The precipitate was washed with 10 mL of light petroleum
(60-90°C) three times and washed with distilled water (3 x 5 mL). The
crude product was air-dried, and the white needles were obtained by
recrystallization from CHCl3 and (CH3)2CO (v/v = 1:1), 1.36 g (yield
81%);
1,22,25-Triacetyl-1,22,25-triaza-3,6:17,20-dibenzo-7,10,13,16-tetraoxoheteroeycleheptaeosane
(1a), 1.36 g (yield 81%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.16 (9H, m,
-CH3), δ = 3.16-3.36 (8H, m, N-CH2C), δ = 3.46-3.56 (4H, m, O-CH2C-O-C),
δ = 3.95 (4H, m, Ar-C-CH2O), δ = 4.13 (4H, m, Ar-O-CH2), δ =4.45 (4H, d,
N-CH2Ar), δ =6.71-7.16 (8H, m, Ar-H). IR (KBr/cm-1): 3443, 2897, 1648,
1609, 1513, 1453, 1416, 1358, 1302, 1239, 980, 830, 807; MS (FAB) m/z:
556 [M + 1]+; anal. calcd. for C30H41N3O7: C, 64.79; N, 7.56; H, 7.43;
found: C, 64.37; N, 7.27; H, 6.98.
