$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for parallel synthesis of ureidothiophene carboxylic
acid library: In a typical run, we realized the reactions with 8
thiaisatoic anhydrides A{1-19} and 10 amines B{1-60}. In a crystallizing
dish intended to one selected amine, we disposed 1 mmole of each of the
eight anhydrides in 8 glass jars. Water (10 ml) was added to give an
aqueous suspension of thiaisatoic anhydride and efficient magnetic
stirring was performed. The addition of 2.2 mmoles of primary or
secondary amines allowed the quick apparition of a solution. Magnetic
stirring was pursued for 2 hours. About 5ml of a 37% hydrochloric acid
solution were then added, the precipitate which was formed was filtered
off and washed with water to give ureidothiophene carboxylic acids.
Analysis by 1H NMR and LC/MS identified successful reaction.
-a1-b1-carbonylaminothiophene-2-carboxylic acid A1B1 C13H11FN2O3S 294.31
g.mol-1 1H NMR : δ = 2.5 (s, 3H, CH3), 6.7 (broad s, 1H, NH), 7.2 (t,
3JHH = 7.8 Hz and 3JHF = 7.9 Hz, 2H, Har), 7.4 (dd, 3JHH = 7.8 Hz and
4JHF = 5.8 Hz, 2H, Har), 7.7 (s, 1H, Hthiophene), 8.3 (broad s, 1H, NH),
12.9 (broad s, 1H, COOH)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, solution phase synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solution-phase parallel synthesis of a 1140-member ureidothiophene
carboxylic acid library
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Le Foulon, Francois-Xavier; Braud, Emmanuelle; Fabis, Frederic; Lancelot,
Jean-Charles; Rault, Sylvain
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Combinatorial Chemistry (2005), 7(2), 253-257

