$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for N-Acylation of Sulfonamides in n-Hexane A mixture
of sulfonamide (1 mmol), carboxylic acid chloride (2 mmol), or carboxylic
acid anhydride (2 mmol) was refluxed in n-hexane (5 mmol) in the presence
of silica chloride (0.3 g) for the appropriate time. The progress of the
reaction was monitored by TLC. After completion of the reaction, the
catalyst was filtered off, and water (10 mL) was added and extracted with
ethyl acetate (2x10 mL). The solvent was evaporated, and the crude
product was purified by column chromatography on silica gel (60-120 mesh,
EtOAc-petroleum ether) or recrystallization (toluene or ethyl
acetate-n-hexane) to afford the pure product. Table 1. Entry 1, yield 80%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, Silica chloride used as solid-support
catalyst
