$DATUM 1314-56-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of N-Butanoyl-4-methyl Benzenesulfonamide: A Typical
Procedure for NAcylation of Sulfonamides under Solvent-free Conditions:
To a vigorously stirred mixture of 4-methyl benzenesulfonamide (0.342 g,
2 mmol) and P2O5/SiO2 [(w/w 75%), 0.35 g], butanoic anhydride (0.632 g, 4
mmol) was added in two portions at 80 °C. The progress of the reaction
was monitored by TLC. After the completion of the reaction, ethyl acetate
(20 ml) was added and the solid materials were removed by filtration. The
filtrate was washed with water (15 ml) and dried over MgSO4. After
evaporation of the solvent, the crude product was purified by
recrystallization from toluene or ethyl acetate/n-hexane mixed solvent to
afford Nbutanoyl-4-methyl benzenesulfonamide. Yield 0.386 g, 80%. m.p.:
82-83 °C, (Lit, 82-83 °C) IR ν (cm-1) 3090, 1680, 1601, 1349, 1158, 1H
NMR (DMSO-d6) δ (ppm) 0.74 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 1.40 (sext, J = 7.3 Hz,
2H), 2.15 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 2.38 (s, 3H), 7.4 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H),
7.79 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 11.99 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (DMSO-d6) δ (ppm) 13.6,
17.95, 21.49, 37.58, 127.95, 129.93, 137.08, 144.54, 171.85.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-catalyst, green chemistry-process simplification,
solid-supported catalyst, no solvent, alternatively reaction carried out
using dichloromethane as solvent, silica-supported P2O5 prepared and used
as catalyst, catalyst recyclable
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM P2O5/SiO2 as an efficient and recyclable catalyst for N-acylation of
sulfonamides under heterogeneous and solvent-free conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Massah, A. R.; Dabagh, M.; Shahidi, S.; Naghash, H. Javaherian; Momeni,
A. R.; Aliyan, H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the Iranian Chemical Society (2009), 6(2), 405-411

