acid chloride (2 mmol), or carboxylic acid anhydride (2 mmol) was
refluxed in n-hexane (5 mmol) in the presence of silica chloride (0.3 g)
for the appropriate time. The progress of the reaction was monitored by
TLC. After completion of the reaction, the catalyst was filtered off, and
water (10 mL) was added and extracted with ethyl acetate (2x10 mL). The
solvent was evaporated, and the crude product was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (60-120 mesh, EtOAc-petroleum ether) or
