$DATUM 67-66-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Methylpyrrolidin-2(3′-piperidyl)amidosuccinic acid (IVb). Succinic
anhydride (1.02 g, 0.01 mol) was added to a solution of 1.70 g (0.01 mol)
of hexahydronicotine in 30 ml of absolute chloroform with mixing and
reactions were left for 5 h. After evaporation of solvent, residues were
separated on silica gel columns by gradient chromatography. Columns were
eluted with a mixture of hexane and chloroform with increasing polarity
The yield was 2.20 g (80%) of IVb as a viscous oil easily soluble in
water and various organic solvents. the boiling point was 71-72°C at 1
mmHg, and nD 20 was 1.4839. The IR spectrum, ν, cm-1, was: 2983-2820
(CHAlk), 2793 (CH3-N), 2750-2730 (COOH), 1714 (C=O), 1643 (C=O), 1470
(CH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and antifungal and antibacterial activity of hexahydronicotine
derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
