$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: N -Acetyl rotaxane 2 A solution of 1 (98 mg,
0.10 mmol), acetic anhydride (19 mL, 0.20 mmol), and triethylamine (70
mL, 0.50 mmol) in N,N-dimethylformamide (0.80 ml) was stirred at 40 °C
for 24 h. The reaction mixture was diluted by dichloromethane, washed by
1 M hydrochloric acid followed by saturated sodium carbonate solution,
dried over magnesium sulfate, and evaporated in vacuo. The crude product
was purified by preparative GPC to give 80 mg (91 %) of 2 as white solid.
10 white solid m.p. 106-107 °C. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, 298 K) δ 8.40 (d,
J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 8.19 (s, 2H), 8.00 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.52-7.49 (m,
1H), 7.40 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 7.30 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.14 (s, 1H),
6.92-6.85 (m, 9H), 6.56 (s, 2H), 5.26 and 5.23 (two s, 2H), 5.26 and 5.23
(two br, 1H), 4.18-4.04 (m, 10H), 3.94-3.62 (m, 10H), 3.26 (br, 4H), 2.88
(br, 4H), 2.70 (br, 4H), 2.28 (s, 6H), 2.24 (s, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (125.7
MHz, CDCl3, 298 K) δ 170.39, 167.11, 166.37, 148.23, 138.25, 138.12,
137.82, 136.37, 136.14, 134.20, 133.54, 132.84, 130.86, 130.69, 129.00,
128.91, 128.38, 127.91, 127.89, 127.10, 126.94, 124.74, 120.66, 120.56,
120.47, 111.42, 69.76, 68.79, 67.71, 67.58, 66.44, 51.35, 46.96, 21.38,
20.84 ppm. IR (KBr) 3439 (ν O-H), 1716 (ν C=O ester), 1639 (ν C=O amide)
cm-1. FAB-MS (m-NBA matrix) m/z 837.5 [M-phthaloyl]+. Anal, calcd for
C58H65NO13·2H2O: C, 68.29; H, 6.82; N, 1.37. found: C, 67.88; H, 6.99; N,
1.30.
