$DATUM 1,22-Di(2-carboxyl-benzoyl)-1,22-diaza-3,6:17,20-dibenzo-7,10,13,16,25-pentaoxoheterocycIoheptacosane
(2c) Compound 2 (1.29 g, 3 mmol) was dissolved in CHCl3 (5 mL), and then
absolute pyridine (2 mL) and phthalic anhydride (1.04 g, 7 mmol) were
added successively. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 12 h.
After the reaction was complete, the solution was poured into 50 mL of
light petroleum ether (60-90°C). The white precipitate formed was
collected by filtration. The precipitate was washed with light petroleum
ether (60-90°C, 3 x 10 mL), and then washed with HCl (0.01 M, 2 x 5 mL)
and distilled water (6 x 5 mL). The crude product was air-dried, and the
white needles were obtained by recrystallization from CHCl3 and (CH3)2CO
(v /v = 1:1), 1.72 g (yield 79%);
1,22-Di(2-carboxyl-benzoyl)-1,22-diaza-3,6:17,20-dibenzo-7,10,13,16,25-pentaoxoheterocycIoheptacosane
(2c), 1.72 g (yield 79%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 3.15 (4H, m,
O-CCH2N), δ = 3.41 (4H, m, O-CH2C-O-C), δ = 3.69 (4H, m, O-CH2-C-N), δ =
3.80 (4H, m, Ar-O-CH2C-O), δ = 4.28-4.38 (4H, m, Ar-CH2N), δ = 6.70-8.70
(16H, m, ArH), δ = 12.90 (2H, s, Ar-COOH). IR (KBr/ cm-1): 3426, 3075,
2927, 2870, 1716, 1634, 1513, 1512, 1456, 1440, 1364, 1294, 1249, 1178,
1117, 1064, 936, 841, 776, 748, 706; MS (ESI positive) m/z: 749.2681,
error = 0.4 ppm [M+Na]+; anal. calcd. for C40H42N2O11: C, 66.16; N, 3.81;
H, 5.68; found: C, 66.12; N, 3.86; H, 5.79.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
