$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: B. A solution of amine 1a-d (0.020 mol) and
maleic anhydride (2.24 g, 0.023 mol) in benzene (100 ml) was heated at
reflux for 10 h to give pure carboxylic acids 2a.
(3aS*,6S*,7R*,7aR*)-6-Bromo-2-(2-furyl-methyl)-1-oxo-1,2,3,6,7,7a-hexahydro-3a,6-epoxyisoindole-7-carboxylic
Acid (2cB); Colorless crystals, yield 78%. Empirical formula:
C14H12BrNO5; Found, %: C, 47.13; H, 3.56; N, 4.22; Calculated, %: C,
47.48; H, 3.42; N, 3.95; Mp: >209°CС (decomp.); IR spectrum, ν, cm-1:
1675 (NCO), 1750 (СО2Н); 1Н NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 2.97 (1Н, d, J
= 8.7, Н); 3.01 (1Н, d, J = 8.7, Н; 3.64 (1Н, d, J = 11.8) and 3.94 (1Н,
d, J = 11.8, 3-CН2); 4.32 (1Н, d, J = 15.6) and 4.50 (1Н, d, J = 15.6,
2-CH2); 6.35 (1Н, dd, J = 0.9, J = 3.1, Н); 6.41 (1Н, dd, J = 1.9, J =
3.1, Н); 6.48 (1Н, d, J = 5.6, Н; 6.74 (1Н, d, J = 5.6, Н; 7.59 (1Н, dd,
J = 0.9, J = 1.9, Н); 13C NMR, δ, ppm: 38.8 (СH2); 47.7 (C-3); 51.1 (Са);
53.0 (C-7); 87.3 (C-3a); 90.5 (C-6); 108.8 (C-4'); 110.6 (C-3'); 138.0
(C-5); 139.8 (C-4); 142.7 (C-5'); 149.8 (C-2'); 169.2 (C-1); 169.6
(CO2H); MS m/z (Irel, %): 353 [М]+ (for 79Br) (3), 274 (27), 254 (19),
228 (17), 194 (70), 176 (76), 159 (52), 148 (29), 131 (47), 109 (38), 96
(72), 80 (100), 67 (26), 53 (88), 43 (65), 32 (34).
