$DATUM 71-43-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(3aR*,6R*,7R*,7aS*)-7,7a-Dichloro-1-oxo-2-phenyl-1,2,3,6,7,7a-hexahydro-3a,6-epoxyisoindole-7-carboxylic
Acid (6a). (General Method). A solution of amine 1e,g,h (0.011 mol) and
dichloro- (1.8 g, 0.011 mol) (for 6a-c) or dibromomaleic anhydride (2.8
g, 0.011 mol) (for 6d) in benzene (20 ml) was stirred for 72 h at 20°C
with monitoring by thin-layer chromatography. The crystalline precipitate
was filtered off and washed with ether (2×15 ml). Recrystallization from
2-propanol-DMF gave the corresponding acids.
(3aR*,6R*,7R*,7aS*)-7,7a-Dibromo-1-oxo-2-phenyl-1,2,3,6,7,7a-hexahydro-3a,6-epoxyisoindole-7-carboxylic
acid (6d); Colorless crystals, yield 76%. Empirical formula:
C15H11Br2NO4; Found, %: C, 42.33; H, 2.13; N, 3.48; Calculated, %: C,
41.99; H, 2.58; N, 3.26; Mp: 175-176°CС; IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 1700
(NCO), 1739 (CO2H); 1Н NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 4.22 (1Н, d, J =
12.5) and 4.58 (1Н, d, J = 12.5, 3-CН2); 5.56 (1Н, d, J = 1.9, Н; 6.73
(1Н, dd, J = 1.9, J = 5.6, Н; 6.77 (1Н, d, J = 5.6, Н; 7.21 (1Н, t, J =
7.5, Н); 7.42 (2Н, br. t, J = 7.5, Н); 7.63 (2Н, br. d, J = 7.5, Н); 13C
