$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,22,25-Tri(3-carboxyl-propionyl)-1,22,25-triaza-3,6:17,20-dibenzo-7,10,13,16-tetraoxoheterocycloheptacosane
(1d) Compound 1 (1.28 g, 3 mmol) was dissolved in CHCl3 (5 mL), and then
absolute pyridine (2 mL) was added. The mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 5 min. After that, butanedioic anhydride (1.00 g, 10
mmol) was added to the solution and stirred at room temperature for 12 h.
After the reaction was complete, the solution was poured into 50 mL of
light petroleum ether (60-90°C). The white precipitate formed was
collected by filtration. The precipitate was washed with light petroleum
(60-90°C) (3 x 10 mL), HCl (0.01 M, 2 x 5 mL), and distilled water (6 x 5
mL), successively. The crude product was air-dried, and the white needles
were obtained by recrystallization from CHCl3 and (CH3)2CO (v/v = 1:1),
1.66 g (yield 76%);
1,22,25-Tri(3-carboxyl-propionyl)-1,22,25-triaza-3,6:17,20-dibenzo-7,10,13,16-tetraoxoheterocycloheptacosane
(1d), 1.66 g (yield 76%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.63 (6H, m,
C-CH2COO), δ = 2.69 (6H, m, CO-CH2-C-CO), δ = 3.16 (8H, m, N-CH2C), δ =
3.71-3.80 (4H, m, C-OCH2C- O), δ = 3.92 (4H, m, Ar-O-C-CH2O), δ = 4.00-
4.15 (4H, m, Ar-OCH2- C-O), δ = 4.38 (4H, m, Ar-CH2N), δ = 6.72-7.79 (8H,
m, Ar-H), δ = 10.52 (3H, s, C-COOH). IR (KBr/cm-1): 3449, 2931, 2872,
1726, 1637, 1513, 1460, 1421, 1362, 1299, 1249, 1174, 1117, 1061, 942,
836, 756, 706; MS (ESI positive) m/z: 752.3001, error = 1.1 ppm [M +
Na]+; anal. calcd. for C36H47N3O13: C, 59.31; N, 5.66; H, 6.36; found: C,
59.26; N, 5.76; H, 6.45.
