$DATUM 1,22-Di(3-carboxyl-propionyl)-1,22-diaza-3,6:17,20-dibenzo-7,10,13,16,25-pentaoxoheterocycloheptacosane
(2d) Compound 2 (1.29 g, 3 mmol) was dissolved in 5 mL of CHCl3, and then
2 mL of absolute pyridine was added. The mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 5 min. After that, butanedioic anhydride (0.70 g, 10
mmol) was added and stirred at room temperature for 12 h. Then the
solvent was poured into 50 mL of light petroleum ether (60-90°C). The
white precipitate formed was collected by filtration. The precipitate was
washed with light petroleum ether (60-90°C, 3 x 10 mL), HCl (0.01 M, 2 x
5 mL), and distilled water (6 x 5 mL), successively. The crude product
was air-dried, and the white needles were obtained by recrystallization
from CHCl3 and (CH3)2CO (v/v= 1:1), 1.66g (yield 76%);
1,22-Di(3-carboxyl-propionyl)-1,22-diaza-3,6:17,20-dibenzo-7,10,13,16,25-pentaoxoheterocycloheptacosane
(2d) 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.62 (4H, m, C-CH2-COO), δ = 2.72 (4H,
m, CO-CH2-C-CO), δ = 3.20 (4H, m, N-CH2-C), δ = 3.37 (4H, m,
C-O-CH2-C-O), δ = 3.49 (4H, m, C-O-CH2-C). δ = 3.71 (4H, m,
Ar-O-C-CH2-O), δ = 4.08 (4H, m, Ar-O-CH2-C-O), δ = 4.48 (4H, m,
Ar-CH2-N), δ = 6.71-7.40 (8H, m, ArH), δ = 10.92 (2H, s, C-COOH). IR
(KBr/cm-1): 3413,2929,2877, 1721, 1618, 1513, 1455, 1418, 1359, 1299,
1250, 1176, 1114, 1062, 940, 834, 761, 707; MS (ESI positive) m/z:
653.2681, error = 1.5 ppm [M + Na]+; anal. ca1cd. for C32H42N2O11: C,
60.89; N, 4.40; H, 6.61; found: C, 60.95; N, 4.44; H, 6.67.
