$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: N-Phthalyl-5-bromanthranilamide (III). To a
solution of 1.10 g (5 mmole) of 5-bromanthranilic acid amide in 15 ml of
ethyl acetate was added with stirring a solution of 0.74 g (5 mmole) of
phthalic anhydride in 15 ml of the same solvent and the mixture was kept
at room temperature for 24 h. The precipitate was filtered, dried, and
recrystallized from dioxane. Compound I, yield, 75%. M.p.,219°C;
Empirical formula: C11H11BrN2O4. 1H NMR spectrum (DMSO-d6): δ, ppm 2.50
(c, 4H, (CH2)2); 7.33 - 8.53 (m, 5H, Harom, NH2); 11.57 (s, 1H, NH);
12.07 (broad signal, 1H, COOH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and the antiinflammatory activity of new
N-acyl-5-bromoanthranilamides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
