$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-Phthalyl-5-bromanthranilamide (III). To a solution of 1.10 g (5 mmole)
of 5-bromanthranilic acid amide in 15 ml of ethyl acetate was added with
stirring a solution of 0.74 g (5 mmole) of phthalic anhydride in 15 ml of
the same solvent and the mixture was kept at room temperature for 24 h.
The precipitate was filtered, dried, and recrystallized from dioxane.
Yield of compound III, 0.64 g (74%). M.p.,196-197°C; Empirical formula:
C15H11BrN2O4; IR spectrum (νmax, cm-1): 3372 (CONH2), 3308 (CONH), 1688
(COOH), 1680 (CONH2), 1670 (CONH), 1590 (CONH2), 1522 (CONH, COOH). 1H
NMR spectrum (DMSO-d6): δ, ppm 7.40 - 8.77 (m, 9H, Harom, NH2); 12.17 (s,
1H, NH); 13.06 (broad signal, 1H, COOH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and the antiinflammatory activity of new
N-acyl-5-bromoanthranilamides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
