$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Monoacylhydrazines 7. Triethylamine (1.46 mL,
10 mmol) was added to a solution of the corresponding oxazolidinone 3 (5
mmol) in chloroform (15 mL). The corresponding acid chloride (10 mmol)
was added under reflux for 30 min. Then the reaction mixture was heated
for 2 h, concentrated, dissolved in toluene, and successively washed with
water, a Na2CO3 solution, and twice with water. Toluene was partially
evaporated, and the product crystallized on cooling. In the case of 7e,
benzene was used instead of chloroform; Ac2O (10 mmol) was immediately
dissolved in benzene (triethylamine was not added). Substrate 3a, which
was subjected to acylation, was added in one portion. The isolation was
carried out as described above.
N-(4-Hydroxy-4,5,5-trimethyl-2-oxooxazolidin-3-yl)acetamide (7e), yield
74% 1H NMR, δ: 1.11 (s, 3 H, 4Me); 1.18 (s, 6 H, 5Me); 1.97 (s, 3 H,
COMe); 6.03 (s, 1 H, OH); 9.90 (s, 1 H, NH). M.p: 182-183°C, Rf (eluent):
0.09, Molecular formula: C8H14N2O4, Found (%): C 47.54, H 6.99, N 13.83;
Calculated (%): C 47.52, H 6.98, N 13.85. M /g mol-1: 202. m/z (Irel (%))
for main lines: 202 (2); 160 (18); 101 (14); 85 (20); 74 (11); 57 (30);
43 (100)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of fused nonaromatic heterocyclic systems based on dioxolanones
and hydrazine
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chudinov, Yu. B.; Gashev, S. B.; Semenov, V. V.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Chemical Bulletin (2006), 55(12), 2238-2246

