$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 2-Acetamidobenzene-1,4-dicarboxylic acid.
2-Acetamidobenzene-1,4-dicarboxylic acid was synthesized following a
slightly modified procedure of Cahn-Speyer:5 2-Aminoterephthalic acid
(1.00 g, 5.52 mmol) was suspended in acetic anhydride (10 mL, 106 mmol)
and heated up to 140 °C. After 10 min a colorless solution was obtained
which was poured into deionized water (300 mL) and left to stand
overnight. Subsequently, a colorless precipitate was filtered off,
recrystallized in water and dried in vacuo. (0.89 g, 3.99 mmol, 72 %). mp
268 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, (CD3)2SO, δ): 2.11 (s, 3 H, CH3), 7.62 (d, 3
J(H,H) = 8.2 Hz, 1 H, Ar H), 8.00 (d, 3 J(H,H) = 8.3 Hz, 1 H, Ar H), 8.95
(s, 1 H, Ar H), 10.95 (s, 1 H, NH), 13.48 (br s, 2 H, COOH); 13C NMR (100
MHz, (CD3)2SO, δ): 25.4, 120.9, 121.5, 123.6, 131.8, 135.7, 141.0, 167.1,
169.2, 169.3; IR (ATR): v = 2358.4 (w), 1674.4 (m), 1575.4 (m), 1525.0
(m), 1467.4 (w), 1415.4 (m), 1373.5 (w), 1328.0 (w), 1299.9 (w), 1248.3
(s), 1129.1 (w), 1081.8 (w), 1017.5 (w), 910.4 (m), 802.9 (w), 753.8 (s),
698.4 (w), 667.5 cm-1 (m); MS (ESI-) m/z (%): 467.07 (35), 355.32 (3),
281.03 (35), 222.04 (100) [M-H]-, 136.04 (85); HRMS (ESI-) m/z: [M-H]-
calcd for C10H8O5N, 222.0407; found, 222.0407; Quantitative Analysis:
Anal. calcd for C10H9NO5: C, 53.82; H, 4.06; N, 6.28. Found: C, 53.28; H,
4.24; N, 6.21.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
